# format.ts
This file provides three formatting helpers for a report renderer: it turns integer-cent amounts into signed, comma-grouped currency strings, converts `YYYY-MM` keys into abbreviated month-and-year labels, and pads text to a requested width with configurable alignment.

## b1
Document the shared purpose of these helpers: report formatting operates on amounts represented as integer cents, while the other utilities format dates and align textual output.

## formatCents
Format an integer-cent `cents` value as a currency string, using `$` by default or the supplied `currency` prefix. Preserve a leading minus sign for negative values, group whole units with `en-US` thousands separators, and always render exactly two digits after the decimal point; for example, `123456` becomes `$1,234.56` and `-5` becomes `-$0.05`.

## formatMonth
Convert a `YYYY-MM` `key` into an `en-US` abbreviated month-and-year label by parsing the year and month and constructing the first day of that month. The returned form is such as `Jan 2024`; the function relies on the input containing a numeric year and month separated by a hyphen.

## pad
Make `text` at least `width` characters wide by adding spaces only when it is shorter than the requested width. Align left by default by appending spaces, or align right by prepending them when `align` is `"right"`; return the original text unchanged when it already meets or exceeds the width.
